      "title": "AzureRM Go Review Rules",
      "introduction": "Apply these rules only when changed lines introduce or expose an actionable defect. Classify the target as legacy untyped Plugin SDK, typed `internal/sdk`, or framework-native before applying model-specific rules. Maintain the existing model unless the change is an explicit migration, and verify Azure API claims against generated SDK models.",
      "sections": [
        { "heading": "Evidence And Implementation Model", "ruleIds": ["IMPL-EVID-001", "IMPL-WF-001A"] },
        { "heading": "Create And Import Behavior", "ruleIds": ["IMPL-WF-002B", "IMPL-WF-002C"] },
        { "heading": "Schema And State", "ruleIds": ["IMPL-SCHEMA-001", "IMPL-SCHEMA-004", "IMPL-SCHEMA-006", "IMPL-SCHEMA-007", "IMPL-SCHEMA-008", "IMPL-SCHEMA-010", "IMPL-SCHEMA-013", "IMPL-SCHEMA-017"] },
        { "heading": "Azure Update Semantics", "ruleIds": ["IMPL-PATCH-001"] },
        { "heading": "Errors", "ruleIds": ["IMPL-ERR-001", "IMPL-ERR-002"] }
      ],
      "closing": "These rules are compact Hosted selections from the implementation compliance contract. Test lifecycle and acceptance-test conventions are deferred to the test supplement so test files do not load duplicate rule meaning."
    },
    {
      "id": "testing",
      "outputPath": ".github/instructions/azurerm-tests.instructions.md",
      "description": "Review Terraform AzureRM provider acceptance tests for lifecycle, harness, assertion, generation, configuration, and callback defects.",
      "applyTo": "internal/**/*_test.go",
      "title": "AzureRM Acceptance-Test Review Rules",
      "introduction": "Apply these rules only when changed lines introduce or expose an actionable test defect. Test files also load the shared Go rules; do not duplicate findings about general Go, schema, API, PATCH, identity, or error behavior.",
      "sections": [
        { "heading": "Evidence And Lifecycle", "ruleIds": ["TEST-EVID-001", "TEST-WF-002", "TEST-WF-002A", "TEST-WF-003", "TEST-WF-004", "TEST-WF-005"] },
        { "heading": "Assertions And Validation", "ruleIds": ["TEST-PATTERN-001", "TEST-PATTERN-002", "TEST-PATTERN-004", "TEST-PATTERN-005", "TEST-PATTERN-006"] },
        { "heading": "Generated And Embedded Content", "ruleIds": ["TEST-PATTERN-008", "TEST-PATTERN-010"] },
        { "heading": "Feature Branches And Azure Setup", "ruleIds": ["TEST-PATTERN-011", "TEST-PATTERN-012"] }
